{
  "$comment": "C-19: the frozen error-code registry. One prefix SKW_, one shape ^SKW_E_<AREA>_<NAME>$, AREA in {RT,DM,SEC,PLT,EXP,PL}. The area is the domain that OWNS the decision, not the layer that reported it. A body is always JSON {error:{code,message?,requestId,detail?}} and never contains a stack, a path, a SQL fragment or a key. scripts/model/validate_schema.py asserts that every SKW_E_* string appearing in schema/*.sql is a member of this file and matches the shape, so a trigger cannot raise a code the app has no mapping for. Adding a code is an edit here plus the app's map; it is not a migration, which is why this is a file and not a table (a table would need a migration per code and could never be the compile-time constant the emitter needs).",
  "version": 1,
  "pattern": "^SKW_E_(RT|DM|SEC|PLT|EXP|PL)_[A-Z0-9_]+$",
